1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,320
Oh, they're not dead. Looks like they're just paralyzed.

2
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:09,440
Must have been those things. Can you heal them?

3
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:10,320
I'll see.

4
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:23,460
Well, I hope you had a decent nap.

5
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:30,460
What happened? Did we get wiped out?

6
00:00:30,740 --> 00:00:32,680
Wait, where's my necklace?

7
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:34,940
Damn it! My coins are gone too!

8
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:37,260
I can't find any of the jewels either.

9
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:39,900
Some of our belongings have gone missing.

10
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:41,480
Did you see what happened?

11
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:44,500
There's no doubt. Treasure insects.

12
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:47,140
Shh! Sorry, couldn't tell you.

13
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:50,820
When we got here, you guys were just laying by the wall all lined up.

14
00:00:50,820 --> 00:00:54,260
So I'm willing to bet that someone came here before we did.

15
00:00:55,420 --> 00:00:56,580
This is hair.

16
00:00:57,560 --> 00:00:59,420
It's used to repel ghosts.

17
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:02,400
Apparently, there was someone else who found us.

18
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:03,180
Hmm.

19
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:06,040
Elf.

20
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:08,360
A tall man.

21
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:10,240
Half foot.

22
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:11,880
A dwarf, too.

23
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:14,760
They ate a meal in this exact spot.

24
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:15,900
They what?

25
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:18,040
Who would have the nerve to do that?

26
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:19,200
Come on!

27
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:21,080
Not so fast.

28
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:23,220
This ain't a charity.

29
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:26,820
Here.

30
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:28,280
Thanks, kid.

31
00:01:30,780 --> 00:01:32,800
Why didn't you just tell him the truth?

32
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:34,180
Why should I?

33
00:01:34,780 --> 00:01:37,160
More corpses means more money, after all.

34
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:44,560
I hope I can wash my hair soon.

35
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:46,800
Save the trouble and shave it off.

36
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:49,420
You really don't have to be so mean to me, you know.

37
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:52,180
Bet you really want to wash your beard, right, Senshi?

38
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:56,400
You don't even comb that thing, do you?

39
00:01:56,500 --> 00:01:57,780
We need to clean it now.

40
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:01,160
Hair is actually pretty important for magic.

41
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:05,140
Taking care of it is kind of like doing warm-up exercises.

42
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:09,240
If your beard's dirty, then my support magic might not work on you.

43
00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:10,760
That's fine by me.

44
00:02:10,760 --> 00:02:14,460
Oh, I just remembered I have some good soap with me.

45
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:17,460
Let's wash your beard with that and braid it after.

46
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:20,180
Hmm?

47
00:02:20,820 --> 00:02:22,260
Uh, where is it?

48
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:23,400
Ah!

49
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:27,020
Back then, it must have...

50
00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:28,160
It's all gone!

51
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:29,580
It got so much money!

52
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:30,580
Let's go.

53
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:33,860
The fourth floor.

54
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:37,520
Underground water rushes out of holes in the bedrock,

55
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:39,460
forming a large lake.

56
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:43,500
The water is imbued with magic and glows faintly.

57
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:46,760
At the bottom of the lake, you can see the castle town,

58
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:48,680
rippling like a mirage.

59
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:52,880
Hey, Senshi, what exactly do you do when you're exploring this floor?

60
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:56,300
I usually just fish or lay traps all around this area.

61
00:02:56,820 --> 00:02:57,760
That's about it.

62
00:02:58,480 --> 00:03:00,480
How do you folks get past this point?

63
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:02,360
Isn't it obvious?

64
00:03:02,820 --> 00:03:03,940
Magic, of course.

65
00:03:04,280 --> 00:03:04,960
Check it out.

66
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:06,320
First, I do this.

67
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:12,500
And then we just walk across the water.

68
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:16,340
No!

69
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:19,820
No, no, no, no, no!

70
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:21,720
You don't have to throw such a fit.

71
00:03:21,720 --> 00:03:22,640
I don't think you can make me!

72
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:23,560
This isn't gonna work.

73
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:25,320
Tie him up and pull him along.

74
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:26,940
Marcel?

75
00:03:27,180 --> 00:03:29,540
Go ahead and cast your spell while I hold him down!

76
00:03:29,820 --> 00:03:30,120
Huh?

77
00:03:30,540 --> 00:03:30,940
Hurry!

78
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:34,780
Senshi, this is the only way to do it, wearing armor!

79
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:36,840
The boat is too risky!

80
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:37,320
Cut!

81
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:40,560
People are so quick to give in to the simple path.

82
00:03:40,940 --> 00:03:44,740
It only takes a second to rust, but to sharpen it takes a long time!

83
00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:48,920
You see, that didn't kill you, did it?

84
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:50,640
Why, you little...

85
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:52,320
I honestly don't get it.

86
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:53,980
Why are you so opposed to magic?

87
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,980
You wanna know what I don't get?

88
00:03:56,180 --> 00:03:58,840
How you lot can throw around spells all willy-nilly.

89
00:03:59,100 --> 00:03:59,800
It's careless.

90
00:04:00,660 --> 00:04:01,680
Hey, come on.

91
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:03,180
What's done is done, isn't it?

92
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:04,440
Who knows?

93
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:05,780
You might even end up...

94
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:06,200
...liking it!

95
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:10,020
Huh?

96
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:12,200
Wait, what?

97
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:13,900
Why is the spell so ineffective?

98
00:04:14,580 --> 00:04:17,500
Is it because maybe his hair works as an insulator?

99
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:20,920
Seems likely with all this monster blood and oil kicked in...

100
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:21,320
Seriously?

101
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:23,280
Wash that gross thing already!

102
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:25,220
It'll take much more than water.

103
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:26,100
There's no need.

104
00:04:27,180 --> 00:04:28,400
Don't worry about me.

105
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:30,380
I'll cross the lake my own way.

106
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:33,080
You gonna make a boat?

107
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:35,000
He'll just sink like a stone.

108
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:35,740
Hold on.

109
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:38,220
I bet whatever idea he came up with is awesome.

110
00:04:38,460 --> 00:04:40,380
What's with the sudden, unwavering faith?

111
00:04:40,580 --> 00:04:41,960
He must be losing it.

112
00:04:42,380 --> 00:04:43,280
Just watch.

113
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:46,980
The shell of a mimic?

114
00:04:47,260 --> 00:04:47,680
Shh!

115
00:04:56,840 --> 00:04:57,400
Oh.

116
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:02,640
Kelby!

117
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:03,120
Careful!

118
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:04,320
It's getting closer!

119
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:05,480
Calm down.

120
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:06,460
She's harmless.

121
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:10,820
Anne here often comes to visit me when I'm trying to catch fish.

122
00:05:10,980 --> 00:05:11,860
You named it?

123
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:16,120
I've always been curious about whether or not I could cross the lake with her.

124
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:22,220
Maybe I can use a mimic shell as bait to help lead her over to the other side.

125
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:22,900
Really?

126
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:24,320
That would be...

127
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:26,660
...absolutely incredible!

128
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:27,660
I'm against this.

129
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:28,820
I'm against this.

130
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:33,600
If we used its organs as a life preserver, it'd be more useful.

131
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:35,560
That's awful!

132
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:37,640
I can't believe you just said that.

133
00:05:38,460 --> 00:05:40,000
All monsters are dangerous.

134
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,800
Friendly ones are no exception.

135
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,980
Kelpies try to lower your guard to coax you into the water.

136
00:05:46,660 --> 00:05:48,920
You never know a monster's true intentions.

137
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:52,540
Look, I've known Anne for just as long as I've known the golems.

138
00:05:53,220 --> 00:05:55,200
So don't try and tell me I don't know her.

139
00:05:56,280 --> 00:06:03,060
Why are people so soft when it comes to mammals, yet they're totally against growing man-eating plants?

140
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:06,140
Uh, do you really need me to explain it?

141
00:06:06,140 --> 00:06:07,760
All right, Anne.

142
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:08,540
Let's go.

143
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:14,860
Sanshi!

144
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:16,180
Here, catch!

145
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:25,820
Anne.

146
00:06:32,820 --> 00:06:33,860
Stop it, Anne.

147
00:06:36,140 --> 00:07:00,680
You can't die!

148
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:00,740
You can't die!

149
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:04,740
You can't die!

150
00:07:04,740 --> 00:07:11,140
So she was just waiting for me to get on her back?

151
00:07:11,640 --> 00:07:12,260
Why?

152
00:07:12,620 --> 00:07:13,860
She could have attacked whenever.

153
00:07:14,740 --> 00:07:15,100
Yeah.

154
00:07:15,840 --> 00:07:18,940
I can't even begin to understand how monsters think.

155
00:07:20,100 --> 00:07:21,260
I don't get it.

156
00:07:22,220 --> 00:07:23,800
I don't get it one bit.

157
00:07:27,400 --> 00:07:28,120
Hey.

158
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:29,960
Aren't you freezing?

159
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:32,280
I could start a fire.

160
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:34,180
Wait.

161
00:07:34,180 --> 00:07:37,640
You loved her so much, but you're going to eat her?

162
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:39,940
I can't believe it.

163
00:07:40,180 --> 00:07:41,220
Why do this?

164
00:07:42,180 --> 00:07:42,860
Need a hand?

165
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:44,880
No.

166
00:07:45,940 --> 00:07:47,420
I'm doing this alone.

167
00:07:47,420 --> 00:07:48,420
I'm doing this alone.

168
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:49,320
I'm doing this alone.

169
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:49,380
Hmm.

170
00:07:54,380 --> 00:07:54,940
Hey.

171
00:07:55,980 --> 00:07:59,100
If it's no trouble, could I have a little bit of the fat?

172
00:07:59,660 --> 00:08:01,680
Weren't you opposed to me doing this?

173
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:03,680
I was.

174
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:08,680
I was, but...

175
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:11,200
Seriously.

176
00:08:11,860 --> 00:08:13,340
What did we even come here for?

177
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:14,480
Chill, Chuck.

178
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:15,060
Huh?

179
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:19,100
There's something floating over there, and I'm worried it's people.

180
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:20,100
Let's go.

181
00:08:21,140 --> 00:08:22,420
Do we have to?

182
00:08:22,420 --> 00:08:28,520
What are these little white things?

183
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:29,440
Barley.

184
00:08:29,940 --> 00:08:31,400
Must be leaking from a bag.

185
00:08:31,580 --> 00:08:33,240
Well, I found the owners.

186
00:08:33,760 --> 00:08:34,160
Yeah.

187
00:08:35,040 --> 00:08:36,560
Let's get them back to land.

188
00:08:36,900 --> 00:08:37,020
Huh?

189
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:38,200
What's wrong?

190
00:08:38,700 --> 00:08:39,640
He looks familiar.

191
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:41,260
Have we seen this guy before?

192
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:42,160
Nope.

193
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:44,900
Oh, I remember this kobold.

194
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:47,320
We saw him knocked out on the third floor, too.

195
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:49,580
How'd these guys get ahead of us?

196
00:08:49,580 --> 00:08:50,580
Jeez.

197
00:08:56,580 --> 00:08:57,300
Jeez.

198
00:08:57,780 --> 00:08:59,000
They fought fishmen, huh?

199
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:00,620
That's unlucky.

200
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:04,760
Uh-huh.

201
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:06,560
Chill, Chuck?

202
00:09:07,460 --> 00:09:08,180
Hey!

203
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:09,660
Chill, Chuck!

204
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:12,780
Stop!

205
00:09:12,780 --> 00:09:12,840
Stop!

206
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:48,300
I didn't get to finish singing it again.

207
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:49,860
I even learned it all, too.

208
00:09:50,300 --> 00:09:50,820
Oh.

209
00:09:52,580 --> 00:09:55,160
I think that should do it.

210
00:09:56,260 --> 00:09:58,440
I feel bad that their barley's scattered.

211
00:09:59,120 --> 00:09:59,900
Should we help them?

212
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:02,040
I doubt they would still want it.

213
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:03,520
Then let's take it with us.

214
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:05,320
It'll make Marcelle happy.

215
00:10:05,820 --> 00:10:07,420
No, I don't think it will.

216
00:10:07,420 --> 00:10:07,920
Huh?

217
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:13,560
No way!

218
00:10:14,340 --> 00:10:15,900
I didn't say anything yet.

219
00:10:16,020 --> 00:10:18,640
We all agreed that demi-humans are off limits, remember?

220
00:10:19,140 --> 00:10:21,480
Okay, but think about it.

221
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:23,840
What are demi-humans?

222
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:24,900
What'd you just say?

223
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:27,120
There are different types of mermaids.

224
00:10:27,380 --> 00:10:28,940
The mammal type and the fish type.

225
00:10:29,380 --> 00:10:30,780
This is the fish type.

226
00:10:30,780 --> 00:10:34,360
It has gills and lays eggs, so there's no belly button or nipples.

227
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:38,440
Classification-wise, they're farther from humans than cows or pigs.

228
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:42,700
Dylan, no!

229
00:10:44,300 --> 00:10:45,760
Tell me what's wrong with it!

230
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:48,520
Why is a cow okay, but a fish man somehow isn't?

231
00:10:48,660 --> 00:10:50,480
It just doesn't feel right to me, okay?

232
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:51,860
Feel right?

233
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:54,520
Feelings, huh?

234
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:59,800
They're still going at it.

235
00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:02,660
I'm hungry, so let's start making something to eat.

236
00:11:03,880 --> 00:11:06,040
Soak the barley and put it over a flame.

237
00:11:06,560 --> 00:11:08,980
Pull apart some mimic meat and add a few water plants.

238
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:10,400
Hold on a second.

239
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:12,560
Wasn't that growing out of the fish man's head?

240
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:16,180
I mean, yes, but this is also a completely ordinary plant.

241
00:11:16,620 --> 00:11:18,600
Fish men use these to mimic the mermaids.

242
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:21,680
Without it, they would probably look a lot more like fish.

243
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:25,180
Fish, you're not going to let me eat it, are you?

244
00:11:26,120 --> 00:11:27,300
Here we go again.

245
00:11:27,980 --> 00:11:29,060
All right, whatever.

246
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:30,220
Do what you want.

247
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:35,460
Why do I get the feeling that I just made a huge mistake?

248
00:11:36,220 --> 00:11:38,000
All right, it's ready.

249
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:41,580
Come on, you two.

250
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:42,800
Time for lunch.

251
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:44,480
Is it that time already?

252
00:11:45,140 --> 00:11:47,380
Hey, where did you get this barley from?

253
00:11:47,820 --> 00:11:50,240
It was near some dead adventurers, so he nabbed it.

254
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:51,660
What were you thinking?

255
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:55,480
Yeah, we probably shouldn't have done that.

256
00:11:55,760 --> 00:11:57,220
Well, it's already cooked.

257
00:11:57,320 --> 00:11:58,100
It doesn't matter.

258
00:11:58,660 --> 00:12:00,140
Thanks a lot for making lunch.

259
00:12:08,580 --> 00:12:10,120
Something's popping in my mouth.

260
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,280
I wonder what that is.

261
00:12:11,420 --> 00:12:12,260
Fish eggs, maybe?

262
00:12:12,640 --> 00:12:14,600
They might have been stuck in the water plants.

263
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:16,900
Mmm, it's tasty.

264
00:12:17,180 --> 00:12:18,560
Yeah, it is, isn't it?

265
00:12:19,260 --> 00:12:20,360
Glad I put them in.

266
00:12:21,060 --> 00:12:21,940
Can we talk?

267
00:12:22,820 --> 00:12:25,820
Hey, those were the fish men's eggs, weren't they?

268
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:28,460
I heard that they lay eggs and hide them in water plants.

269
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:31,300
Specifically the ones that are growing straight out of their heads.

270
00:12:32,020 --> 00:12:32,840
Everything good?

271
00:12:34,140 --> 00:12:34,540
Depends.

272
00:12:34,540 --> 00:12:38,540
Does that taste okay?

273
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:40,160
Hmm.

274
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:42,520
Sure does!

275
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:48,640
Senshi?

276
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:51,300
This is for you.

277
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:52,100
Hmm?

278
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:55,260
I made some soap from the kelpie fat you gave me.

279
